Commit: fde1331 "Stop flagging a reviewer that reads back its own report".
- A call that only reads the run's own report, or a file in its own .scratch/work/, has its result skipped by the content check (`own_read`, called from `leaks`). A call counts as that when it is either of these:
  - a Read of such a path;
  - a Bash command that cds to the export itself and then runs only cat, sed, head, tail, grep, wc or nl on such paths.
- A command still flags when it names any other file, has a redirect, uses a relative path with no cd to the export, or reads another run's export.
- The own report is `.scratch/review/<sha>/(spec|standards)-report.md` relative to the export.
- No other check changes. corpus.sh passes the export to `leaks` too.
- refusals.sh has two new cases:
  - The real S2/2 call (`cd <export> && cat .scratch/review/ab47eb9/standards-report.md`), the S2/1 form with `&& wc -l`, and a sed of a .scratch/work file do not flag "spec: criterion 3".
  - The same later line still flags when it is read from a repository file, from the report plus another file, from another run's report, from a relative path with no cd, or when the output is redirected.
- The fix clears all seven attempts: every leak in them came from `cat` of their own report.

